{"id": "zsfg-patient-credit-balance-corrections", "title": "San Francisco General understated patient receivables by $21.6 million", "seconds": 45.0, "voice": "tinyvoca:F2", "narrator": "Temporary local narration", "made": "2026-11-28", "key": "9eb7ac07cd3ec762", "words": 132, "beats": [{"scene": "p", "kind": "compare", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "A hospital credit can mean a refund is due, or that a billing code needs fixing.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.5, "shot": "s0", "visual": {"type": "compare", "rows": [["June 2019", "$17.3 million"], ["June 2020", "$31.3 million"]]}}, {"scene": "p", "kind": "compare", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "At San Francisco General, those credits reached 31.3 million dollars.", "t0": 4.62, "t1": 9.58, "shot": "s1", "visual": {"type": "compare", "rows": [["June 2019", "$17.3 million"], ["June 2020", "$31.3 million"]]}}, {"scene": "p", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "That was up from 17.3 million dollars the year before.", "t0": 9.7, "t1": 13.25, "shot": "s2", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "original", "kicker": "Patient credits grew 81 percent", "text": "$17.3 million", "mark": "$17.3"}}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The hospital traced about 21.6 million dollars to coding and other adjustments.", "t0": 13.47, "t1": 18.29, "shot": "s3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$21.6 million", "label": "The adjustment belonged in two years"}}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Eight million belonged to the opening balance.", "t0": 18.41, "t1": 20.67, "shot": "s4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "original", "kicker": "The adjustment belonged in two years", "text": "Opening balance", "mark": "Opening"}}, {"scene": "b", "kind": "compare", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Another 13.6 million belonged to the year’s patient revenue.", 